    <footnotes>
        <footnote id="F1">Disposed of pursuant to the Agreement and Plan of Merger, dated as of October 8, 2026, by and among Pacira BioSciences, Inc. (&quot;Issuer&quot;), Viatris Inc. (&quot;Viatris&quot;) and Peach Purchaser Sub Inc. (&quot;Purchaser&quot;) (the &quot;Merger Agreement&quot;), pursuant to which Purchaser consummated a cash tender offer (the &quot;Offer&quot;) to purchase all of the outstanding shares of Issuer's common stock (the &quot;Shares&quot;) for $36.50 per Share, net of applicable withholding taxes and without interest (the &quot;Offer Price&quot;), after which Purchaser merged with and into Issuer with Issuer continuing as the surviving corporation and a wholly owned subsidiary of Viatris (the &quot;Merger&quot;). On November 17, 2026, the effective time of the Merger (the &quot;Effective Time&quot;), each Share was converted into the right to receive the Offer Price.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F2">Includes 1,022.077 Shares acquired under the Issuer's Amended and Restated 2014 Employee Stock Purchase Plan in June  2026.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F3">Includes restricted stock unit awards (&quot;RSUs&quot;). Pursuant to the Merger Agreement, at the Effective Time, each RSU that was outstanding as of immediately prior to the Effective Time, whether vested or unvested, was canceled and converted into the right to receive an amount in cash equal to the product of (i) the total number of Shares issuable in settlement of such RSU, multiplied by (ii) the Offer Price, subject to applicable tax withholdings.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F4">Pursuant to the Merger Agreement, at the Effective Time, each option to purchase Shares (&quot;Option&quot;) that was outstanding as of immediately prior to the Effective Time, whether vested or unvested, was canceled and converted into the right to receive an amount in cash equal to the product of (i) the total number of Shares subject to such Option immediately prior to the Effective Time, multiplied by (ii) the excess, if any, of (A) the Offer Price minus (B) the exercise price payable per Share under such Option, subject to applicable tax withholdings. Each Option that was outstanding immediately prior to the Effective Time which had a per Share exercise price greater than or equal to the Offer Price was cancelled at the Effective Time with no consideration payable.</footnote>
    </footnotes>

